{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Infra.DirichletL","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.DirichletCharacter.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.ZetaValues","lean:module:QOU.Infra.Polylogarithm"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3_holds","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L80-L96","doc":"**`β(3) = π³/32`, proved.**  From Mathlib's Fourier series of the\nBernoulli polynomial `B₃` (`hasSum_one_div_nat_pow_mul_sin`, `k = 1`) at\n`x = 1/4`: `B₃(1/4) = 3/64`, and `sin(2πn/4) = χ₄(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.sin_quarter_eq_chi4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.sin_quarter_eq_chi4","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L64-L78","doc":"`χ₄` read off the sine: `sin(2πn/4) = χ₄(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.beta3IsLChi4_3","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L53-L62","doc":"**`β(3) = π³/32`**, stated as the convergent Dirichlet series\n`Σ_{n ≥ 1} χ₄(n) / n³ = π³ / 32`, i.e. `L(χ₄, 3) = π³/32` (Euler).\n\nUntil 2026-11-15 this was `def beta3IsLChi4_3 : Prop := True`, on the\nstated ground that `β` and `L(χ, s)` are not Mathlib objects here.  The\nseries needs neither: it is a `HasSum` over `ℕ`, and the `n = 0` term is\n`χ₄(0)/0³ = 0/0 = 0` in Lean's division, so it contributes nothing.\nBean `qou-35zi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.chi4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.chi4","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L47-L51","doc":"`β(3) = L(χ_4, 3)` instance (the chief Catalan-like example).\nHere `χ_4` is the unique non-trivial character mod 4 satisfying\n`χ_4(-1) = -1`; specialised at depth 3 gives Catalan's β(3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.hurwitz_lerch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.hurwitz_lerch","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The Hurwitz-Lerch decomposition holds at every depth `n ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.DirichletLClass","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L32-L45","doc":"**Hurwitz-Lerch decomposition (axiomatic form).**\n\nEncodes the manuscript identity\n\n  `L(χ, n) = N^{-n} Σ_{a=1..N-1} χ(a) · ζ_H(n, a/N)`\n\nvia the relation between `L(χ, n)` and the Hurwitz zeta values\n`ζ_H(n, a/N)`.  The full statement is conditional on\n`Polylogarithm.TheoremA` (which identifies the cyclotomic\npolylog values) plus the Gauss-sum identity on `χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.DirichletL.lValueAxiomatic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.DirichletL.lValueAxiomatic","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/DirichletL.lean#L22-L30","doc":"Axiomatic Dirichlet L-value `L(χ, n)` for a character `χ mod K`\nand integer `n ≥ 2`.  Encoded as an *axiomatic real number*\nparameterised by the character data (here: just `K` and the\nlist of character values, supplied as a function\n`chi : ℕ → ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}